e graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques","title":"MaximalCliques","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximalCliques()":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximalCliques","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order; see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MaximalCliques"},{"type":"text","text":" for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order. Self-loops and parallel edges are ignored, and an isolated vertex is a clique of one."}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximalcliques()","title":"maximalCliques()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximalCliques()","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","title":"Cliques","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol"}}}